<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace faithfully reproduces Coiled molluscs in general; the six panels are labelled cf. Nautilus, Turritella, an ammonite, Conus, Cerithium, Helix (resemblance, not specimens) morphology" ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) create_raup_animations.py, 1966-raup.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Coiled molluscs in general; the six panels are labelled cf. Nautilus, Turritella, an ammonite, Conus, Cerithium, Helix (resemblance, not specimens) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 64.1/100, audit 2026-10-17-raup-audit) and the assessments." ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/1966-raup.py; output: raup_shell_animation.gif; organism: Coiled molluscs in general; the six panels are labelled cf. Nautilus, Turritella, an ammonite, Conus, Cerithium, Helix (resemblance, not specimens); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/ba6fd20; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; other sources: Geometric analysis of shell coiling: coiling in ammonoids <https://pubs.geoscienceworld.org/jpaleontol/article-abstract/41/1/43/80199/geometric-analysis-of-shell-coiling-coiling-in>" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2014.08.010>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/srep42445>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.138.3537.150>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.147.3663.1294>,
        <https://doi.org/10.2307/1301992> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-raup-audit-raup-shell-coiling-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-raup-audit-raup-shell-coiling-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-raup-audit-raup-shell-coiling-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-raup-audit-raup-shell-coiling-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-raup-audit-raup-shell-coiling-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-raup-audit-raup-shell-coiling-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-raup-audit-raup-shell-coiling-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-raup-audit-raup-shell-coiling-specimen-match> ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 6.41e-01 .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-raup-audit-raup-shell-coiling-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace — Code-to-model traceability: 75/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The docstring maps each parameter to its definition and its line of code, the generating function is commented line by line with the identity each line enforces, the self-test names what it excludes, and the parameter sets carry a note on why each value. Not higher because the equations are tied to the secondary sources' notation rather than to numbered equations of Raup 1966. Evidence: create_raup_animations.py L81–L107: raup_shell() docstring and comments <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L81-L107>; 1966-raup.py L1–L18: equations in the module docstring <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/1966-raup.py#L1-L18>; datasets/raup/README.md L32–L52: the model as a table: symbol, equation, meaning <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/datasets/raup/README.md#L32-L52>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-raup-audit-raup-shell-coiling-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace — Model fidelity to source: 80/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The three parameters now mean what Raup's model says they mean, and the script proves it on its own output: W is the per-revolution magnification of every dimension, D the inner/outer-margin ratio of the generating curve, T the axial over radial movement of its centre, and the generating curve lies in the plane through the axis, so the shells are self-similar tubes rather than flat ribbons. The three defects of the first version are each named in the docstring and each is excluded by the self-test. Not higher because the primary paper was not consulted: the definitions are taken from two secondary restatements (which agree with each other on W, D and T up to Noshita's 2/(1+D) scaling of T, which is noted), the direction of the S ratio is the repository's convention rather than Raup's, and Raup's generating curve is an arbitrary aperture outline, here always an ellipse. Evidence: create_raup_animations.py L20–L36: the four parameters defined, with the equations <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L20-L36>; create_raup_animations.py L96–L104: raup_shell(): a, r_c, z_c, generating curve in the radial-axial plane <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L96-L104>; create_raup_animations.py L38–L45: the three defects of the first version and how each is now excluded <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L38-L45>; create_raup_animations.py L134–L157: self_test(): recovery to 1e-9, spire monotone in T, planispiral one aperture thick <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L134-L157>; 1966-raup.py L28–L37: the same generating function in the minimal script <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/1966-raup.py#L28-L37>; datasets/raup/variables.json L134–L140: mathematical_formulation: the equations as implemented, with their source <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/datasets/raup/variables.json#L134-L140>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-raup-audit-raup-shell-coiling-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace — Morphometric validation: 45/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Shape quantities are now measured on the rendered geometry - W, D and T recovered from each mesh, height/width and spire/width per panel - written to a CSV, printed, shown on the still, and re-derived independently in the measurements sidecar; recovered values equal the inputs to 5e-15 in the script's own check and, in the sidecar's independent derivation, exactly for W and T and to 3e-4 for D (the aperture's inner margin is read off a 100-point grid). That is validation of the implementation against the definitions, and it is complete. What the dimension also asks for - a comparison with specimens or with the paper's own figures - is absent: no published W, D, T of a real shell, and none of Raup's block-diagram placements, is compared with anything here. Evidence: create_raup_animations.py L110–L131: recover_parameters(): W, D, T, height/width, spire/width from the mesh <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L110-L131>; create_raup_animations.py L189–L204: write_metrics(): the CSV <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L189-L204>; raup_shell_metrics.csv (generated output, not in repo): six rows, nominal and recovered values — raup_shell_metrics.csv: rendered output of create_raup_animations.py at ba6fd20, text/csv, 483 B, sha256 384d298d81f5373f754f790c2fa6560b93f8cf9164028a160b4df80810680057. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): recovered translation rate T, 'Planispiral' (W=3.0, D=0.0, T=0.0) = 0.0 ratio (reference 0.0, Raup's definition of T (dz_c/dr_c), Noshita 2014 / Okabe & Yoshimura 2017; should equal the input) [Δz_c / Δr_c of the generating-curve centre over the last revolution of raup_shell()] — height/width = 0.629, spire/width = 0.000; recovered distance from axis D, 'Planispiral' (W=3.0, D=0.0, T=0.0) = 0.0003 ratio (reference 0.0, Raup's definition of D; should equal the input) [inner margin / outer margin of the aperture (min/max radial distance of the last generating curve)]; recovered whorl expansion W, 'Planispiral' (W=3.0, D=0.0, T=0.0) = 3.0 ratio (reference 3.0, Raup's definition of W; should equal the input) [centre distance from the axis at the aperture / one revolution earlier]; recovered translation rate T, 'Turreted' (W=1.3, D=0.05, T=3.5) = 3.5 ratio (reference 3.5, Raup's definition of T (dz_c/dr_c), Noshita 2014 / Okabe & Yoshimura 2017; should equal the input) [Δz_c / Δr_c of the generating-curve centre over the last revolution of raup_shell()] — height/width = 1.142, spire/width = 0.858; recovered distance from axis D, 'Turreted' (W=1.3, D=0.05, T=3.5) = 0.0502 ratio (reference 0.05, Raup's definition of D; should equal the input) [inner margin / outer margin of the aperture (min/max radial distance of the last generating curve)]; recovered whorl expansion W, 'Turreted' (W=1.3, D=0.05, T=3.5) = 1.3 ratio (reference 1.3, Raup's definition of W; should equal the input) [centre distance from the axis at the aperture / one revolution earlier]; recovered translation rate T, 'Evolute disc' (W=2.0, D=0.45, T=0.0) = 0.0 ratio (reference 0.0, Raup's definition of T (dz_c/dr_c), Noshita 2014 / Okabe & Yoshimura 2017; should equal the input) [Δz_c / Δr_c of the generating-curve centre over the last revolution of raup_shell()] — height/width = 0.321, spire/width = 0.000; recovered distance from axis D, 'Evolute disc' (W=2.0, D=0.45, T=0.0) = 0.4501 ratio (reference 0.45, Raup's definition of D; should equal the input) [inner margin / outer margin of the aperture (min/max radial distance of the last generating curve)]; recovered whorl expansion W, 'Evolute disc' (W=2.0, D=0.45, T=0.0) = 2.0 ratio (reference 2.0, Raup's definition of W; should equal the input) [centre distance from the axis at the aperture / one revolution earlier]; recovered translation rate T, 'Conical' (W=3.5, D=0.0, T=1.5) = 1.5 ratio (reference 1.5, Raup's definition of T (dz_c/dr_c), Noshita 2014 / Okabe & Yoshimura 2017; should equal the input) [Δz_c / Δr_c of the generating-curve centre over the last revolution of raup_shell()] — height/width = 0.805, spire/width = 0.481; recovered distance from axis D, 'Conical' (W=3.5, D=0.0, T=1.5) = 0.0003 ratio (reference 0.0, Raup's definition of D; should equal the input) [inner margin / outer margin of the aperture (min/max radial distance of the last generating curve)]; recovered whorl expansion W, 'Conical' (W=3.5, D=0.0, T=1.5) = 3.5 ratio (reference 3.5, Raup's definition of W; should equal the input) [centre distance from the axis at the aperture / one revolution earlier]; recovered translation rate T, 'High-spired' (W=1.6, D=0.1, T=2.5) = 2.5 ratio (reference 2.5, Raup's definition of T (dz_c/dr_c), Noshita 2014 / Okabe & Yoshimura 2017; should equal the input) [Δz_c / Δr_c of the generating-curve centre over the last revolution of raup_shell()] — height/width = 0.998, spire/width = 0.738; recovered distance from axis D, 'High-spired' (W=1.6, D=0.1, T=2.5) = 0.1002 ratio (reference 0.1, Raup's definition of D; should equal the input) [inner margin / outer margin of the aperture (min/max radial distance of the last generating curve)]; recovered whorl expansion W, 'High-spired' (W=1.6, D=0.1, T=2.5) = 1.6 ratio (reference 1.6, Raup's definition of W; should equal the input) [centre distance from the axis at the aperture / one revolution earlier]; recovered translation rate T, 'Globose' (W=3.0, D=0.1, T=1.0) = 1.0 ratio (reference 1.0, Raup's definition of T (dz_c/dr_c), Noshita 2014 / Okabe & Yoshimura 2017; should equal the input) [Δz_c / Δr_c of the generating-curve centre over the last revolution of raup_shell()] — height/width = 0.628, spire/width = 0.341; recovered distance from axis D, 'Globose' (W=3.0, D=0.1, T=1.0) = 0.1002 ratio (reference 0.1, Raup's definition of D; should equal the input) [inner margin / outer margin of the aperture (min/max radial distance of the last generating curve)]; recovered whorl expansion W, 'Globose' (W=3.0, D=0.1, T=1.0) = 3.0 ratio (reference 3.0, Raup's definition of W; should equal the input) [centre distance from the axis at the aperture / one revolution earlier]." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:hasProbability 4.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-raup-audit-raup-shell-coiling-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace — MorphoEval overall 64.1/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "raup_shell(W, D, T, S) sweeps an ellipse of radial semi-axis a = a0 W^(theta/2pi) and axial semi-axis a/S, centred at r_c = a(1+D)/(1-D) from the axis and z_c = T r_c along it, in the plane through the axis. self_test() recovers W, D, T from meshes on a 3x3x4 grid to 4.9e-15 and checks the spire's axial travel rises strictly with T (the outer height/width may stay flat while the last whorl still envelops the spire, which is correct behaviour for involute forms); a T=0 shell is checked to be exactly one aperture thick. Six illustrative panels (W, D, T from variables.json) rendered rotating in side and overhead view; W x D and W x T sheets; a six-panel still with height/width; a CSV of nominal and recovered W, D, T per panel with height/width and spire/width. The measurements sidecar recovers W, D, T again, independently, from the script's generating function. Overall 64.1/100 (faithfulness 58.6, reproducibility 77.0); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit ba6fd20; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 80, Morphological realism / specimen match 45, Parameter expressivity 70, Morphometric validation 45, Source and data traceability 75, Code-to-model traceability 75, Reproducibility package 80. Output judged: raup_shell_animation.gif: rendered output of create_raup_animations.py at ba6fd20, image/gif, 15189434 B, 1200×800 px, 100 frames, sha256 986555a0032be189233cbf0ec15193959bf7f9cc0b1e099a6b7a289f7cff8b02." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling> ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Obtain Raup 1966 and pin the definitions of W, D, T, S to its equations and figures; confirm the direction of the S ratio.",
        "remediation needed: Put a real shell beside at least one panel - a photograph, or a specimen's measured (W, D, T) from Raup 1967's ammonoid table or a later gastropod dataset - and measure the agreement.",
        "remediation needed: Report the stored frame count after saving the GIF, or write it with a writer that does not merge frames.",
        "remediation needed: Sweep S and D on their own in the parameter sheet; mark Raup's block-diagram regions (gastropods, ammonoids, bivalves, brachiopods) on the W x T and W x D sheets once the paper is in hand." ;
    pk:hasProbability 6.41e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-raup-audit-raup-shell-coiling-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace — Parameter expressivity: 70/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Each of W, D, T now has its own visible monotone effect, shown on two sheets (W x D at fixed T, W x T at fixed D) and on the 3 x 3 W x T slice of 1966-raup.py, and the self-test asserts the T effect. S is exposed in the function but not swept in any figure, and D is swept only together with W rather than on its own; the ranges on the sheets are the dataset's indicative bounds, not Raup's. Evidence: create_raup_animations.py L236–L259: create_parameter_space_visualization(): the two sheets <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L236-L259>; 1966-raup.py L40–L71: W x T slice at fixed D <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/1966-raup.py#L40-L71>; create_raup_animations.py L147–L151: spire_over_width strictly increasing in T asserted <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L147-L151>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-raup-audit-raup-shell-coiling-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace — Reproducibility package: 80/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Deterministic (no RNG), no external data, a CLI with --frames, --fps, --no-gif, --self-test-only and --out-dir, a self-test that runs before any drawing and fails loudly, outputs that fill their panels, and the minimal script runs headless with --no-show/--out. numpy, matplotlib and Pillow are in requirements.txt and pinned in requirements.lock.txt. Not higher because the GIF is 16 MB and 100 frames for a 7 s loop, and because Pillow silently merges 20 of the 120 rendered frames, which the script does not report. Evidence: create_raup_animations.py L280–L300: main(): CLI, self-test first <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L280-L300>; create_raup_animations.py L178–L183: fit_axes(): panels filled <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L178-L183>; 1966-raup.py L40–L44: --no-show / --out <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/1966-raup.py#L40-L44>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling-repro-package> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-raup-audit-raup-shell-coiling-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace — Source and data traceability: 75/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Raup 1962, 1965 and 1966 are cited with DOIs (the 1966 JSTOR id, wrong in the dataset since 2025, is corrected), the two secondary sources the definitions actually come from are cited with DOIs and the specific statement used from each is given, and the dataset says plainly which of its earlier contents could not be verified and why they were replaced. Not higher because the primary paper was not read, so nothing here is pinned to a page or equation of Raup 1966, and because the parameter sets and ranges are the author's illustrative choices with no external source. Evidence: create_raup_animations.py L6–L18: citation block with DOIs; which definitions come from which secondary source <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L6-L18>; datasets/raup/README.md L1–L30: revision notice: what was unverifiable and what replaced it <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/datasets/raup/README.md#L1-L30>; datasets/raup/variables.json L10–L10: revision_2026_10_17 provenance note <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/datasets/raup/variables.json#L10-L10>; datasets/raup/paper_citations.bib L1–L70: DOIs added; JSTOR 1301992 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/datasets/raup/paper_citations.bib#L1-L70>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling-source-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-raup-audit-raup-shell-coiling-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace — Morphological realism / specimen match: 45/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The six forms are now distinct and each is what its name says (spire/width 0.00 for the two planispirals, 0.86 for the turreted form, 0.74 high-spired, 0.48 conical, 0.34 globose), and the panel titles and a figure footnote say that the taxon names are resemblances, not specimens. But there is still no real shell in the figure and no measured specimen the panels are tested against, which is what the dimension asks for; the labels are honest, not validated. Scored above the 30 of the first audit because the forms are no longer wrong, below the midpoint because nothing checks that a Turritella looks like the turreted panel. Evidence: raup_empirical_comparison.png (generated output, not in repo): six panels, each a different form; footnote on provenance — raup_empirical_comparison.png: rendered output of create_raup_animations.py at ba6fd20, image/png, 562658 B, 1630×1070 px, sha256 c50dbee57d0a64950d5470aed25583817eb8d39b97bcf2a7b89b991973f63ef7; raup_shell_animation.gif (generated output, not in repo): side view: a tower, a cone, a disc, an involute coil; overhead: the log spirals — raup_shell_animation.gif: rendered output of create_raup_animations.py at ba6fd20, image/gif, 15189434 B, 1200×800 px, 100 frames, sha256 986555a0032be189233cbf0ec15193959bf7f9cc0b1e099a6b7a289f7cff8b02; create_raup_animations.py L174–L176: ILLUSTRATIVE: the footnote text <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L174-L176>; datasets/raup/variables.json L66–L133: the six parameter sets with a note on why each value <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/datasets/raup/variables.json#L66-L133>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasProbability 4.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling> rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace faithfully reproduces Coiled molluscs in general; the six panels are labelled cf. Nautilus, Turritella, an ammonite, Conus, Cerithium, Helix (resemblance, not specimens) morphology" ;
    dct:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" .

